              "content": "kilograms. A newborn blue whale weighs around 2,700 kg, which is similar to the weight of an adult hippopotamus. The heart of a blue whale was recorded to be nearly 700 kg. The tongue of a blue whale weighs as much as an elephant. Blue whales can eat up to 3500 kg of krill every day. The largest known land animal, Argentinosauras, is estimated to weigh 90,000 kgs."
